#: admin/class-modules-data.php:872
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Open All External Links in New Tab"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:873
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid ""
"Ensure that all external links within post content open in a new browser tab by implementing the "
"\"target=\"_blank\"\" attribute. Additionally, enhance security and SEO advantages by including the "
"\"rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\"\" attribute."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:876
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Allow Menu Custom Links to Open in New Tab"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:877
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid ""
"You can enable custom link menu items to open in a separate browser tab with just a simple checkbox. "
"Additionally, to reinforce security and improve SEO performance, we've implemented the \"rel=\"noopener "
"noreferrer nofollow\"\" attribute for these links."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:880
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Auto-Publish Posts with Missed Schedule"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:881
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid ""
"Automatically initiate the publication of scheduled posts marked with \"missed schedule\" upon each visit to "
"the website, across all post types."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:884
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Code Snippets"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:885
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid ""
"Add custom code snippets to your website without the need to edit the theme's functions.php file. This "
"feature is especially useful for adding custom CSS, JavaScript, and PHP code to your website. For disable all "
"snippets, add this line to your wp-config.php: define('WPMASTERTOOLKIT_SNIPPETS_SAFE_MODE', true);"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:888
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Disable Comments"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:889
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid ""
"Manage the visibility of comments on your public posts by selectively disabling them for specific post types "
"or across all posts. Once comments are disabled, any existing comments will seamlessly disappear from the "
"front-end."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:892
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Disable Feeds"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:893
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid ""
"Completely deactivate RSS, Atom, and RDF feeds across your website. This entails disabling feeds for various "
"content elements, such as posts, categories, tags, comments, authors, and search. Additionally, it erases any "
"remaining references to feed URLs from the <head> section of your web pages."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:896
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Disable Gutenberg"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:897
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid ""
"Deactivate the Gutenberg block editor selectively, allowing you to control its usage for specific or all "
"relevant post types."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:900
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Disable wp_mail"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:901
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid ""
"Disable the wp_mail function, which is used by WordPress to send emails. This feature is useful for websites "
"that do not send emails, as it prevents the wp_mail function from loading and consuming resources."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:904
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Hide WordPress Version"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:905
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid "Hide the WordPress version from the source code."
msgstr ""

