#: admin/class-modules-data.php:972
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Manage Admin Emails Notifications"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:973
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid "Check the types of emails you no longer want to receive as an administrator."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:976
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Disable WP Sitemap"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:977
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid "Disable the default WordPress sitemap feature, which was introduced in WordPress 5.5."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:980
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Force Send All Email To"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:981
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid ""
"Force all emails sent from your website to be sent to a specific email address. This feature is useful for "
"testing email functionality on your website, as it ensures that all emails are sent to a single email address."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:984
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Plugin Download"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:985
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid "Download plugins from the plugins page in the WordPress admin panel."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:988
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Disallow Malicious File Access in upload"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:989
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid "Protect your website from malicious file access in the upload directory."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:992
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Disable cart fragments scripts"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:993
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid ""
"Disable cart fragments scripts on the front-end for public site visitors. This might break the functionality "
"of the cart and checkout pages if they depend on cart fragments."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:996
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Revisions Control"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:997
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid ""
"Avoid overloading the database by setting a cap on the number of revisions to save for certain or all types "
"of posts that support revisions."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1000
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Disable emoji support"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1001
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid ""
"Disable emoji support for pages, posts and custom post types on the admin and frontend. The support is "
"primarily useful for older browsers that do not have native support for it. Most modern browsers across "
"different OSes and devices now have native support for it."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1004
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Disable dashicons CSS and JS files"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1005
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid ""
"Disable loading of Dashicons CSS and JS files on the front-end for public site visitors. This might break the "
"layout or design of custom forms, including custom login forms, if they depend on Dashicons. Make sure to "
"check those forms after disabling."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1008
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Disable WordPress shortlink <link> tag"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1009
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid ""
"Disable the default WordPress shortlink <link> tag in <head>. Ignored by search engines and has minimal "
"practical use case. Usually, a dedicated shortlink plugin or service is preferred that allows for nice names "
"in the short links and tracking of clicks when sharing the link on social media."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1012
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Disable Really Simple Discovery (RSD) <link> tag"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1013
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid ""
"Disable the Really Simple Discovery (RSD) <link> tag in <head>. The RSD tag is used by XML-RPC clients to "
"discover the location of the XML-RPC endpoint on your site. If you don't use XML-RPC, you can safely disable "
"this tag."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1016
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Disable Windows Live Writer (WLW) manifest <link> tag"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1017
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid ""
"Disable the Windows Live Writer (WLW) manifest <link> tag in <head>. The WLW app was discontinued in 2017."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1020
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Disable Block-Based Widgets Settings Screen"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1021
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid ""
"Disable block-based widgets settings screen. Restores the classic widgets settings screen when using a "
"classic (non-block) theme. This has no effect on block themes."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1024
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Custom Body Class"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1025
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid "Add custom <body> class(es) on the singular view of some or all public post types."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1028
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Redirect After Logout"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1029
msgctxt "Module description"
