msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1033
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid "Set custom redirect URL for all or some user roles after login."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1036
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Wider Admin Menu"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1037
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid "Give the admin menu more room to better accommodate wider items."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1040
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Disable Dashboard Widgets"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1041
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid ""
"Clean up and speed up the dashboard by completely disabling some or all widgets. Disabled widgets won't load "
"any assets nor show up under Screen Options."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1044
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Disallow Bad Requests"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1045
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid ""
"Protect your site against a wide range of threats. check all incoming traffic and quietly blocks bad requests "
"containing nasty stuff like eval(, base64_, and excessively long request-strings."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1048
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Auto Regenerate Salt Keys"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1049
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid "WordPress salt keys or security keys are codes that help protect important information on your website."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1052
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Hide PHP Versions"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1053
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid ""
"Some servers send a header called X-Powered-By that contains the PHP version used on your site. It may be a "
"useful information for attackers, and should be removed."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1056
msgctxt "Module name"
msgid "Nav Menu Visibility"
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1057
msgctxt "Module description"
msgid "Control your nav menu by allowing you to apply visibility controls to menu."
msgstr ""

#: admin/class-modules-data.php:1060
msgctxt "Module name"
