#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:432
msgid ""
"Add security headers quickly to your site to protect it from threats such as phishing attacks, data theft and "
"more."
msgstr ""

#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:438
msgid "Resolve duplicate site headers"
msgstr ""

#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:444
msgid ""
"When a website loads, the server sends headers (small pieces of information) to the browser that tell it how "
"to handle the content and security settings of the site. Sometimes, the same header can be sent more than "
"once (duplicated) either due to misconfiguration or conflicts between plugins, themes, or server settings. "
"These duplicate headers can cause issues like: Slower website loading times, Confusion in how browsers "
"interpret security or content rules, Potential conflicts that can make certain features of the site not work "
"properly."
msgstr ""

#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:454
msgid "Disable (Strict-Transport-Security)."
msgstr ""

#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:462
msgid "Disable (Permissions-Policy)."
msgstr ""

#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:470
msgid "Disable (X-Content-Type-Options)."
msgstr ""

#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:478
msgid "Disable (X-Frame-Options)."
msgstr ""

#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:486
msgid "Max-Age"
msgstr ""

#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:492
msgid ""
"It is advisable to set \"max-age\" to a high value, such as a full year (31536000 seconds). This ensures that "
"browsers continue to store security information for a long period of time, which helps protect users from man-"
"in-the-middle attacks. However, it is important to keep in mind that setting the value too high could cause "
"problems if you need to change your site's SSL configuration in the future. Therefore, it is important to "
"carefully consider your usage and security needs before setting the value."
msgstr ""

#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:500
msgid ""
"The Max-Age parameter specifies the period of time (in seconds) for which the browser should store the HSTS "
"information."
msgstr ""

#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:506
msgid "Include Subdomains"
msgstr ""

#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:512
msgid ""
"We recommend enabling the \"includeSubDomains\" option in the HSTS header to ensure that all subsections of "
"your site (subdomains) are only loaded via HTTPS. However, before enabling this flag, it is important to "
"ensure that all subdomains, resources and web services working under your domain are available via HTTPS and "
"that there are no compatibility issues with any external services used by your site."
msgstr ""

#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:522
msgid "Enable include subdomains"
msgstr ""

#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:525
msgid ""
"The \"includeSubDomains\" flag specifies that the effect of the header should also be applied to subdomains "
"of the domain."
msgstr ""

#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:531
msgid "Preload"
msgstr ""

#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:537
msgid ""
"Enabling \"preload\" further helps prevent any potential man-in-the-middle attacks, thus improving connection "
"security as far as it concerns HSTS. Please note that even if this flag is enabled, your website still needs "
"to be manually submitted to the list. Please also note that inclusion in the preload list has permanent "
"consequences and is not easy to undo, so you should only enable this flag and submit your website after "
"making sure that all of the resources and services within your domain (and its subdomains, if "
"\"includeSubDomains\" is also enabled) are indeed accessible and functional via HTTPS."
msgstr ""

#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:547
msgid "Enable preload"
msgstr ""

#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:550
msgid "The \"preload\" flag allows the website to be included in the HSTS preload list."
msgstr ""

#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:556
msgid "CSP Header Contents"
msgstr ""

#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:562
msgid ""
"The Content Security Policy (CSP) header is a security feature used to prevent various types of attacks on "
"websites, like cross-site scripting (XSS), clickjacking, and data injection attacks. It does this by "
"controlling which resources (such as scripts, images, styles, or media) the browser is allowed to load and "
"execute."
msgstr ""

#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:570
msgid ""
"HTTP Content-Security-Policy header controls website resources, reducing XSS risk by specifying allowed "
"server origins and script endpoints."
msgstr ""

#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:576
msgid "CSP Report URI"
msgstr ""

#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:582
msgid ""
"The CSP Report URI is a directive within the Content Security Policy (CSP) header that tells the browser "
"where to send reports when a violation of the CSP occurs. Instead of blocking resources outright, this "
"directive can be used to monitor potential security issues on your site without disrupting users by reporting "
"violations to a specified URL."
msgstr ""

#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:590
msgid "Enter your custom URL (Sentry, URIports, Datadog, and Report URI) for CSP violation reports."
msgstr ""

#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:595
msgid "Permissions Policy Contents"
msgstr ""

#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:600
msgid ""
"The HTTP Permissions-Policy header provides a mechanism to allow and deny the use of browser features in a "
"document or within any <iframe> elements in the document."
msgstr ""

#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:605
msgid "X-Frame-Options"
msgstr ""

#: admin/modules/core/class-protect-website-headers.php:617
msgid ""
"The X-Frame-Options HTTP response header can be used to indicate whether or not a browser should be allowed "
"to render a page in a <frame>, <iframe>, <embed> or <object>. Sites can use this to avoid click-jacking "
"attacks, by ensuring that their content is not embedded into other sites."
msgstr ""

